{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill","id":100174,"title":"Kill la Kill","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-27T10:59:16-07:00","id":100174,"title":"Kill la Kill","content":"Kamui senketsu<br /> Kamui junketsu<br /> Shinra Koketsu<br /> <br /> the 5 goku 3 stars ultra uniforms<br /> the 1 and 2 stars goku uniforms<br /> <br /> the scissors<br /> bakuzan<br /> <br /> wich type of artifacts should fit these ones<br /> and wich type of exaltation (or entity) do you think they are (including ragyo and her crew)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:39:58-07:00","id":100204,"title":"","content":"Satsuki Kiryuin is Dragon-Blooded, or at least where I think a competent Dragon-Blooded character should be in a fight that's mostly between Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> She started out as the rival but it became increasingly clear that she's simply wasn\u2019t on Ryuko's level, the important part is that she's fine with that because her main strength is in the bonds of trust and loyalty she has with the Four Devas (her Sworn Brotherhood) and the infrastructure she was able to build in the Kiryuin family\u2019s name.<br /> <br /> I'm so used to anime characters (especially female ones) who aren't at the highest power level basically going &quot;well I'm of no use to anyone anymore!&quot; its very refreshing to see a weaker character remain useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T11:51:35-07:00","id":100216,"title":"","content":"i like the fact that she is able to get junketsu at his full potential not being like ragyo or ryuko, and i want to know where did she found bakuzan and the history behind that katana (dual ko-dachis atm)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:45:25-07:00","id":100261,"title":"","content":"The way Ryuko and Satsuki gradually master the power of their Kamuis is something that Evocations will model really, really well. Same thing for the scissor blade, though to a lesser extent. <br /> <br /> Assigning Exalt types is kind of tricky.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Ryuko is probably the hardest to pin down, but given her back story and motivation I would pin her as an Abyssal. She could easily be represented as something else though.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Mako is a Chosen of Serenity, or maybe Ryuko's Lunar mate.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Satsuki would make a great Zenith Caste; I'd attribute her relative weakness compared to Ryuko and Ragyo as them outstripping her in Essence.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Four Devas + Iori definitely work as a sworn brotherhood of Dragon-Blooded. Gamagoori's an easy pick for Earth. Inumuta seems like a Water Aspect, given his skills as an intelligence gatherer, criminal mastermind, and giant battleship pilot. Wood seems obvious for Nonon since it has Performance but my intuition say it fits Sanageyama better; I think Nonon would work well as a Fire Aspect who favors Performance. Iori, who's passively sitting back and handling the R&amp;D end of things when he's not leading covert strikes, probably works as an Air Aspect.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Ragyo works well as an Infernal, although she could be an immensely powerful Exigent of the life fibers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nui is probably spot-on for a Liminal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:28:22-07:00","id":100292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100261#post100261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2022 Nui is probably spot-on for a Liminal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would see her as a fairly powerful Demon-blood myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:39:22-07:00","id":100300,"title":"","content":"for me, ragyo looks more like an akuma, and after todays chapter, nui is, i dont know, seems like a biofibers amalgam, or some kind of powerfull homunculous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:40:24-07:00","id":100301,"title":"","content":"I'd personally make Ryuko, Satsuki and Ragyo all Solars. Ryuko might need a couple of custom Charms and Ragyo a lot, but that's to be expected in adapting media and otherwise Solars can easily fit all three thematically. I'd agree Satsuki is getting out-Essenced (or maybe just freaking loves the Bureaucracy cascade and isn't keeping up in Melee).<br /> <br /> Mako I'd probably use as an Exigent (I say with less confidence, not knowing how they work). Her spotlight/hallelujah routine is <i>something</i>, and she can clearly use artifacts, but she doesn't have the excellence of the Exalted as we're used to them and isn't supposed to. I'd suggest she started life as a minor Ally on Ryuko's sheet and playing her was shared around the group troupe-style, building up a ridiculous string of awesome running jokes until she was everyone's favourite character. Gamagoori's player is trying to buy her from Ryuko's <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nui is a monster, as ST I'd reskin liberally from all over the place and make some kind of custom beast that was never intended to be PC-OK. Who knows, maybe 3rd will have some cool behemoth rules?<br /> <br /> Everyone (<b>everyone</b>) is ridiculously more resilient than they would be in Exalted, but I think dealing with that satisfactorily in the 3rd Ed rules would be much easier than in earlier editions. I can think of a few levers to pull offhand.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2474-mengtzu","name":"Mengtzu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2474_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:56:40-07:00","id":100318,"title":"","content":"I know I'm opening the flood gates... But what's so special about this anime? Because people seem to love it. Should I be interested in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:01:55-07:00","id":100321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100318#post100318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm opening the flood gates... But what's so special about this anime? Because people seem to love it. Should I be interested in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's by Trigger (of Gurren Lagann fame), has a rad animation budget, really cool action scenes, and a well-rounded cast of likable characters. It's got some pretty egregious male gaze and sexual objectification which brings it down, but if you can stomach that, it is fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:04:18-07:00","id":100324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100321#post100321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's by Trigger (of Gurren Lagann fame), has a rad animation budget, really cool action scenes, and a well-rounded cast of likable characters. It's got some pretty egregious male gaze and sexual objectification which brings it down, but if you can stomach that, it is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... It's from the guys who did Gurren Lagann?... I'll be back in a... However long it takes to watch it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:18:25-07:00","id":100334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100324#post100324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's... It's from the guys who did Gurren Lagann?... I'll be back in a... However long it takes to watch it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A while, the anime finished earlier today. We're just waiting on the subs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:36:09-07:00","id":100351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100324#post100324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's... It's from the guys who did Gurren Lagann?... I'll be back in a... However long it takes to watch it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't expect anything even close to the same level of quality, though. At all. Fair warning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:43:59-07:00","id":100355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100321#post100321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's by Trigger (of Gurren Lagann fame), has a rad animation budget, really cool action scenes, and a well-rounded cast of likable characters. It's got some pretty egregious male gaze and sexual objectification which brings it down, but if you can stomach that, it is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. When I first heard about the series it sounded interesting, but then I saw the &quot;costumes&quot;: <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/4/47703/3353430-0319655912-686033.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/...12-686033.jpeg</a><br /> <br /> Couldn't bring myself to watch it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:59:06-07:00","id":100365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100355#post100355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. When I first heard about the series it sounded interesting, but then I saw the &quot;costumes&quot;: <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/4/47703/3353430-0319655912-686033.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/...12-686033.jpeg</a><br /> <br /> Couldn't bring myself to watch it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The outfits get a bad rap but the girls aren't actually sexualized all that much compared to shows like Ikkitousen or Strike Witches. When they are it's usually to make a point about something else like Ragyo's extremely creepy familial relationships, and the guys arguably spend more time naked than the girls do.<br /> <br /> Seriously, Aikuro by himself generates more lady-service than five or six episodes of Free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:01:51-07:00","id":100367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100318#post100318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm opening the flood gates... But what's so special about this anime? Because people seem to love it. Should I be interested in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>- All the awesome of an incredibly long action anime squeezed into 24 episodes with no filler.<br /> <br /> - Bold and distinct visuals; when the studio has to cut corners to save budget, it's almost always stylish enough to get away with it.<br /> <br /> - Cool characters of both genders, but the heights of power, agency and awesomeness belong to women.<br /> <br /> - Awesome soundtrack.<br /> <br /> - Odd but interesting setting.<br /> <br /> - Mako<br /> <br /> - As Vance says, definite problematic content. There's a probably legitimate but ultimately tedious argument along the lines of &quot;there's artistic merit to what they're trying to do with the fanservice&quot; and &quot;yes but they're obviously trying to have that cake and eat it too&quot;. I think the anime easily has enough points overall that it can sustain the deserved penalty and should be watched anyway. I would suggest extreme caution in buying merchandise.<br /> <br /> Most of all, while FATE and its ilk are probably strictly better than Exalted for emulating it, KLK is very much reminiscent of how lots of us ran our 1E games, the system's actual pacing be damned. Thus as an Exalted fan it fires you right up, and Ex3's combat system is superb fuel for that fire (again, not exactly the same but a great deal of the feel is right). I think you could make a pretty satisfying Ryuko as a starting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2474-mengtzu","name":"Mengtzu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2474_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:01:56-07:00","id":100368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100351#post100351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't expect anything even close to the same level of quality, though. At all. Fair warning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I the only one who finds Kill la Kill superior to Gurren Lagann?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://s67.photobucket.com/user/EggmanSizzle/media/Ex3KSBadge_zps950331e7.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i67.photobucket.com/albums/h311/EggmanSizzle/Ex3KSBadge_zps950331e7.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"http://s67.photobucket.com/user/EggmanSizzle/media/BackerBadgesmall_zps424a0237.png.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i67.photobucket.com/albums/h311/EggmanSizzle/BackerBadgesmall_zps424a0237.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/846-eggmansizzle","name":"eggmansizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:14:15-07:00","id":100385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eggmansizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100368#post100368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I the only one who finds Kill la Kill superior to Gurren Lagann?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Gurren Lagann got my blood pumping in ways that Kill La Kill doesn't. It's a good series but everything up to the final episode (which I haven't seen yet, so mind your spoilers) has been merely good instead of &quot;holy shit this is the most amazing thing I've ever seen.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:18:22-07:00","id":100388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100385#post100385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Gurren Lagann got my blood pumping in ways that Kill La Kill doesn't. It's a good series but everything up to the final episode (which I haven't seen yet, so mind your spoilers) has been merely good instead of &quot;holy shit this is the most amazing thing I've ever seen.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See, reverse those titles and that's my reaction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://s67.photobucket.com/user/EggmanSizzle/media/Ex3KSBadge_zps950331e7.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i67.photobucket.com/albums/h311/EggmanSizzle/Ex3KSBadge_zps950331e7.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"http://s67.photobucket.com/user/EggmanSizzle/media/BackerBadgesmall_zps424a0237.png.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i67.photobucket.com/albums/h311/EggmanSizzle/BackerBadgesmall_zps424a0237.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/846-eggmansizzle","name":"eggmansizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:21:11-07:00","id":100391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eggmansizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100368#post100368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I the only one who finds Kill la Kill superior to Gurren Lagann?</div> </div> </div> </div>for me, gurren lagann was more fluid and more interesting than KLK, that doesnt mean KLK wasnt fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:25:58-07:00","id":100396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100365#post100365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Aikuro by himself generates more lady-service than five or six episodes of Free.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is played for comedy. The girls, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:27:32-07:00","id":100398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eggmansizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100368#post100368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I the only one who finds Kill la Kill superior to Gurren Lagann?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kill la Kill has a weaker beginning, but TTGL's ending was weak. Looking forward to seeing how KLK ends tonight.<br /> <br /> For those wondering whether to watch it: take Gurren Lagann, strip out most of the blatant phallic symbolism and exploration of the nature and meaning of independence, and replace it with blatant yonic symbolism and exploration of the nature and meaning of dependence. It's still from a male perspective, and it shows, but it comes across to me as Trigger's attempt to wrap their minds around how they feel about female sexuality, while putting all of that in the skin of a fanservicey action title. Watch it only if you can take a) total sensory overload, and b) waiting sixteen (out of 24) episodes for the plot to crystallize into something recognizable.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh right, Exalted: It's my personal belief that Ryuko is a Lunar protagonist, with Satsuki acting as her Solar Mate (a Zenith, most likely). Also, as Zan pointed out to me, Satsuki and the Four Devas/Elite Four correspond pretty well to a perfect Solar Circle.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Mako's a Chosen of Serenity on celestial cocaine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 03-27-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:32:38-07:00","id":100401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100396#post100396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is played for comedy. The girls, not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aikuro is always played for comedy, Ryuko is often played for comedy when she's not being played for drama, and Satsuki is so sexually-intimidating that not even the mother of all fanservice outfits can strip her of her dignity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:38:48-07:00","id":100406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bascially everyone</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something something, people getting butthurt, something something, a giant fucking crusade, something something...</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Sigh&gt; Americans...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100398#post100398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill la Kill has a weaker beginning, but TTGL's ending was weak. Looking forward to seeing how KLK ends tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weak? You're seriously telling me that the ending to Gurren Lagann was <i>weak</i>? God damn it, they were tossing galaxies at each other by the end. I wouldn't exactly call the ending to Gurren Lagann <i>weak</i>. Amazing, yeah. Fucking awesome, sure. But not weak. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-27-2014, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:42:59-07:00","id":100410,"title":"","content":"On which characters are played for comedy:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I just realized that the only characters never played for comedy are Kiryuins. Once it's revealed that Ryuko is one, she stops being played for comedy too.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:55:33-07:00","id":100418,"title":"","content":"Ah whoops, my mistake, maybe Episode 24 won't be the last? (Edit: It totally was.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100406#post100406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weak? You're seriously telling me that the ending to Gurren Lagann was <i>weak</i>? God damn it, they were tossing galaxies at each other by the end. I wouldn't exactly call the ending to Gurren Lagann <i>weak</i>. Amazing, yeah. Fucking awesome, sure. But not weak. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a lot of flash, with very little substance. The answer to every problem, in the end, was &quot;try harder&quot; and &quot;eschew compromise.&quot; This wasn't very satisfying, especially in comparison to the climax of the first season.<br /> <br /> TTGL was comparable to Creation's First Age: a seemingly-neverending string of victories, which were at first inspiring and later disappointing because there's nothing to learn from infinite victory. This is why Exalted is set in the Second Age: because victory is not assured, and because the excesses and failures of the past aren't simply going to be avoided because the protagonist says so. A hard-won victory, earned over a lifetime, is more deeply satisfying than any amount of galaxy-punching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 03-28-2014, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:57:16-07:00","id":100422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100418#post100418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah whoops, my mistake, maybe Episode 24 won't be the last?<br /> <br /> It was a lot of flash, with very little substance. The answer to every problem, in the end, was &quot;try harder&quot; and &quot;eschew compromise.&quot; This wasn't very satisfying, especially in comparison to the climax of the first season.<br /> <br /> TTGL was comparable to Creation's First Age: a seemingly-neverending string of victories, which were at first inspiring and later disappointing because there's nothing to learn from infinite victory. This is why Exalted is set in the Second Age: because victory is not assured, and because the excesses and failures of the past aren't simply going to be avoided because the protagonist says so. A hard-won victory, earned over a lifetime, is more deeply satisfying than any amount of galaxy-punching.</div> </div> </div> </div>It captured the essence of Japanese culture for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:05:34-07:00","id":100436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100418#post100418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah whoops, my mistake, maybe Episode 24 won't be the last?<br /> <br /> It was a lot of flash, with very little substance. The answer to every problem, in the end, was &quot;try harder&quot; and &quot;eschew compromise.&quot; This wasn't very satisfying, especially in comparison to the climax of the first season.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to every problem was &quot;never stop looking for a solution.&quot; Because cynicism is for losers and doesn't accomplish anything, while optimism opens doors in your mind and makes many things possible that a cynic would insist cannot be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:34:25-07:00","id":100460,"title":"","content":"While a &quot;can do&quot; attitude is important, the problem is that the answer you cited sells the show itself short. The whole point of the villains was that endless, heedless ambition and optimism necessarily causes its own problems, which the series repeatedly showed throughout its run... right up until the end. What was the solution to the problem that ambition breaks things? Worry about the details later. Not, &quot;find a clever solution,&quot; or &quot;find some way to compromise with the Anti-Spirals for our mutual benefit.&quot; Just... more power, and everything will work out, even though it's been established that spiral power's problems are self-reinforcing.<br /> <br /> The reason the ending was weak was because the earlier parts of the show had <i>character</i>. People faced difficult choices, people lost, and a good man died because of his dear friend's stupid decisions. The setting was presented as complex, and the final conflict ignored that in favor of bigger special effects. If I'd seen this ending in a less well-written anime, I would have had no real complaints other than &quot;Eh, that's shonen anime for you.&quot; But TTGL's writing grew weaker toward the end, compared to its strong middle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:46:57-07:00","id":100463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100460#post100460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a &quot;can do&quot; attitude is important, the problem is that the answer you cited sells the show itself short. The whole point of the villains was that endless, heedless ambition and optimism necessarily causes its own problems, which the series repeatedly showed throughout its run... right up until the end. What was the solution to the problem that ambition breaks things? Worry about the details later. Not, &quot;find a clever solution,&quot; or &quot;find some way to compromise with the Anti-Spirals for our mutual benefit.&quot; Just... more power, and everything will work out, even though it's been established that spiral power's problems are self-reinforcing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That was the entire point of Nia's death and Simon's refusal to just spiral her back to life. Just because you can do the impossible doesn't mean you should. The solution to spiral nemesis is tempering unlimited power with the wisdom to know when not to use it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:55:55-07:00","id":100466,"title":"","content":"I can totally support you on that, HK-87. I just wish the actual climax had covered that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:41:49-07:00","id":100491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100321#post100321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's by Trigger (of Gurren Lagann fame), has a rad animation budget, really cool action scenes, and a well-rounded cast of likable characters. It's got some pretty egregious male gaze and sexual objectification which brings it down, but if you can stomach that, it is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn you Trigger for making something so good that i'll stomach the fanservice <br /> <br /> The sound track is really awesome too. Hiroyuki Swanano is great<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T18:42:52-07:00","id":100522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eggmansizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100368#post100368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who finds Kill la Kill superior to Gurren Lagann?</div> </div> </div> </div> No, you are not. I enjoyed both series, but I enjoyed Kill la Kill much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T19:03:17-07:00","id":100534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100491#post100491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sound track is really awesome too. Hiroyuki Swanano is great</div> </div> </div> </div>Kill la Kill's soundtrack is worth listening to even if you've never seen the anime. Every refined prince of Hell needs to walk into the room to the strains of <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oWhcTesRFq0\" target=\"_blank\">Blumenkranz</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T19:20:27-07:00","id":100544,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, though, that while not completely balanced this show does better in terms of equal-opportunity fanservice than most, even if a good deal of the female-oriented fanservice is played for comedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T19:24:58-07:00","id":100547,"title":"","content":"The Kamuii transformation stock-footage sequences are often uncomfortable, because even when cut down for time, they always include the ass and crotch shots. (Later on, circumstances make the transformations more heartwarming, because they signify the bonds between the major characters. Of course, these are full sequences that don't focus on the uncomfortable bits.)<br /> <br /> However, after the first two or three episodes have dealt with Ryuuko's embarrassment about the skimpiness and the leering of the male audience, the fact that she and Satsuki are half-naked fades into the background. Maybe the camera stops focusing on Tits and Ass as part of the &quot;don't allow others to objectify you&quot; lesson Satsuki gives Ryuuko, or maybe one just grows desensitized. Possibly both.<br /> <br /> I know that I stop caring when the camera is more focused on the fact that Ryuko and Satsuki are now superhumans whose clashes casually take to the skies, shatter concrete and create air vaccuums. Or at least, that's the content that stuck with me -- the action and the dialogue.<br /> <br /> <br /> By comparison, the Three-Star Uniform transformations are almost never uncomfortable. For one thing, three of the Four Devas are male, and the naked part sequence for the female is exactly the same as the males (save for a cute little &quot;magical girl pose&quot;), which focus on any specific part of her anatomy.<br /> <br /> I <i>am </i>disappointed that her final battle form is by far the skimpiest of the four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T19:41:28-07:00","id":100557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100547#post100547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, after the first two or three episodes have dealt with Ryuuko's embarrassment about the skimpiness and the leering of the male audience, the fact that she and Satsuki are half-naked fades into the background. Maybe the camera stops focusing on Tits and Ass as part of the &quot;don't allow others to objectify you&quot; lesson Satsuki gives Ryuuko, or maybe one just grows desensitized. Possibly both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did it <i>ever</i> do that? I can think of maybe two or three ass shots in the whole series outside the transformation sequences. Maybe I'm just desensitized by more blatant shows. I definitely don't remember anything like the zoom-in panty shots from Strike Witches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T20:10:58-07:00","id":100569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100557#post100557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it <i>ever</i> do that? I can think of maybe two or three ass shots in the whole series outside the transformation sequences. Maybe I'm just desensitized by more blatant shows. I definitely don't remember anything like the zoom-in panty shots from Strike Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tennis fight was... pretty bad. Granted, I haven't watched beyond that, because the level of objectification in the second episode alone skeeved me out too much to keep watching, but <i>wow</i> there were extended leering and camera pan sequences in that fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T20:29:04-07:00","id":100576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100557#post100557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it <i>ever</i> do that? I can think of maybe two or three ass shots in the whole series outside the transformation sequences. Maybe I'm just desensitized by more blatant shows. I definitely don't remember anything like the zoom-in panty shots from Strike Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that comes to mind are the long, slow progressions up Ryuuko's body whenever a boy is ogling her like a bloody moron. That happens twice in the same episode, where the transformed Kamui is first seen on scene. I don't recall it happening again.<br /> <br /> Any ass-shots I might remember have the butt in the foreground, but your attention is probably on the opponent in-focus in the background, who is talking. But then, I'm working off someone's photoshopped comparison of two characters' butts; no telling if the shots were focused on the butt or if that was just image-cropping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T21:01:11-07:00","id":100591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100534#post100534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill la Kill's soundtrack is worth listening to even if you've never seen the anime. Every refined prince of Hell needs to walk into the room to the strains of <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oWhcTesRFq0\" target=\"_blank\">Blumenkranz</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome. That music makes me laugh stupidly it's so awesome.<br /> <br /> Also, this thread caused me to start watching Kill la Kill a few hours ago, and I'll probably watch GL afterwards... never seen them before, so thank you, Forum.<br /> <br /> Edit* ....oh...and thanks for the Blumenkranz. &gt;.&gt; now I'm going to spend the next few days pissing myself off trying to learn it on the piano.<br /> <br /> Edit2* Dammit. I got too absorbed in the show and a dog ate my tuna sandwich. Cursed canines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","user":"Arteliex","date":". 03-28-2014, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T23:02:30-07:00","id":100617,"title":"","content":"On fanservice in Kill la Kill:<br /> <br /> Kill la Kill has plenty of man-service to go with the fanservice.<br /> <br /> While there is objectification of women going on in the show, Trigger was perfectly willing to objectify guys too and is rather more equal opportunity than the vast majority of Japanese shows are. By the end of the show <i>everybody</i> had stripped down multiple times and gotten plenty of shots of their bodies. The camera tended to linger a bit more on the girls, but then the guys tended to run around totally butt naked rather often. And both the fanservice and manservice were often directly called out and commented on by characters within the show.<br /> <br /> Plus the whole idea of clothing, nudity and being comfortable with who you are, were major themes in the show, so it's not like the fan/man-service was totally gratuitous, existing <i>only</i> to get more bucks. It actually did have a place in the greater context and narrative of the show. The reason why Ryuuko's outfit looks the way it does makes perfect sense once they explain how things are actually working.<br /> <br /> So I think it generally evens itself out, and I wish more shows bothered to work their &quot;fanservice&quot; into the story as well as Kill la Kill did.<br /> <br /> <br /> On Kill la Kill vs Gurren Lagann:<br /> <br /> I found Gurren Lagann tended to slow down quite a bit in the middle of the two major arcs. Kill la Kill pretty much had the same level of energy going from episode 1 to episode 24. While it didn't hit the highs of Gurren Lagann, it didn't hit the lows either. I did find Gurren Lagann more unpredictable. In Kill la Kill most of the twists I saw coming, though they tended to do them in ways that I wasn't expecting.<br /> <br /> I find the two shows about equal all told, and I think Kill la Kill was a fantastic show for an original series from a brand new animation company. Between Little Witch Academia and Kill la Kill, I can't wait to see what Trigger does in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> On Kill la Kill and Exalted:<br /> <br /> I think Ragyo fits eerily well as a Reclamation oriented Infernal.<br /> <br /> Satsuki is definitely a Zenith.<br /> <br /> The Devas (+ tailor guy) fit really nicely as a circle of Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Takarada is the hero Creation needs.<br /> <br /> From an out-of-game perspective Nui isn't bad as a Raksha - the way she shows up and starts warping the story, and the way she feels like a character who is a little bit outside of the story but trying to get into it (which mirrors her relationship with Satsuki and Ryuuko). She also seems to have the &quot;Craziest&quot; powers. It also fits a bit with what happens in the final episode where:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">She uses Assumption of the Person's Heart to fuse with Ragyo.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ryuuko is the only one I have a tough time deciding on. She fits pretty nicely as any of the Exalted types, though her penchant for bleeding everywhere does make me think about an Abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-28-2014, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T00:32:03-07:00","id":100634,"title":"","content":"Have people stoped watching porn while I was away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T01:03:21-07:00","id":100639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quot