-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100728#post100728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is Nui's not on this list? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>adding her song (and laughing like a mad scientist while looking at my antagonist npcs)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T11:34:52-07:00","id":100809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100617#post100617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an out-of-game perspective Nui isn't bad as a Raksha -</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, thinking more about this at work last night, I realized that while her narrative might be a bit reflective of a Fair Folk, mechanically she is a Scourge Caste Infernal so hard it hurts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Many of the powers she exhibits can be mimicked with Adorjan charms. Her ability to create clones, her power to fly, her insane dodging skills. She even uses Loom Snarling Deception in episode 13; of course instead of creating a false destiny in the Loom for her, it creates an entire fake student history for her in <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> Honnouji Academy's database; and all that information unravels the moment she stops using her char- err, the moment she stops using her power.</span></span><br /> <br /> Further many of the statements she makes in the series are pretty reflective of an Adorjani mindset - &quot;Love and hate are two sides of the same coin,&quot; or, &quot;A lady forgets her past when she changes her underwear.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T13:37:55-07:00","id":100853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100634#post100634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have people stopped watching porn while I was away?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100727#post100727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, ok, it's worth the hype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was basically my sequence of events too, from, &quot;This looks awful&quot; to &quot;This is awesome!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T14:13:20-07:00","id":100873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100853#post100853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, this was basically my sequence of events too, from, &quot;This looks awful&quot; to &quot;This is awesome!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand. I asked if people stoped watching porn, because I was getting tired of people who can't accept that some stories have the audacity to use nudity as a medium.<br /> <br /> I was highly intrigued from the get go, in fact. When I first saw Ryuuko in her Majo Shoujo mode I noticed she was blushing. Which seemed strange because generally, for some ungodly reason, anime characters don't recognize the fact that they're 80% naked, but she seemed to be actually uncomfortable with it. And sure enough, it turns out it's a story element. So why would people get butthurt over that is beyond me.<br /> <br /> If anything, the only thing that's weird is the teacher guy's habit of breaking into sexualized posses. Which, <i>I assume</i> he's doing for a reason, otherwise it doesn't make eny sense. Don't get me wrong, he's sexy and all, but it just reminds me of Queen's Blade a little too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-28-2014, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T14:29:39-07:00","id":100877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100873#post100873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was highly intrigued from the get go, in fact. When I first saw Ryuuko in her Majo Shoujo mode I noticed she was blushing. Which seemed strange because generally, for some ungodly reason, anime characters don't recognize the fact that they're 80% naked, but she seemed to be actually uncomfortable with it. And sure enough, it turns out it's a story element. So why would people get butthurt over that is beyond me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it's in vogue that everyone has to be ultra-sensitive about gender issues and we're perpetuating some great injustice against women unless we hunt down and burn every last portrayal of women that is even vaguely sexualized. Or something. And if we complain about guys being sexualized too then that gets dismissed as &quot;male wish fulfillment.&quot; Which thankfully isn't an argument I've heard used against this series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T14:33:55-07:00","id":100878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100877#post100877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably because it's in vogue that everyone has to be ultra-sensitive about gender issues and we're perpetuating some great injustice against women unless we hunt down and burn every last portrayal of women that is even vaguely sexualized. Or something. And if we complain about guys being sexualized too then that gets dismissed as &quot;male wish fulfillment.&quot; Which thankfully isn't an argument I've heard used against this series.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're at it, let's burn books for having <i>written text</i>, everybody knows it's fucking witchcraft<br /> <br /> \u200bFuck that. Like seriously, fuck that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-28-2014, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T15:16:54-07:00","id":100896,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100261#post100261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way Ryuko and Satsuki gradually master the power of their Kamuis is something that Evocations will model really, really well. Same thing for the scissor blade, though to a lesser extent.<br /> <br /> Assigning Exalt types is kind of tricky.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Ryuko is probably the hardest to pin down, but given her back story and motivation I would pin her as an Abyssal. She could easily be represented as something else though.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Mako is a Chosen of Serenity, or maybe Ryuko's Lunar mate.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Satsuki would make a great Zenith Caste; I'd attribute her relative weakness compared to Ryuko and Ragyo as them outstripping her in Essence.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Four Devas + Iori definitely work as a sworn brotherhood of Dragon-Blooded. Gamagoori's an easy pick for Earth. Inumuta seems like a Water Aspect, given his skills as an intelligence gatherer, criminal mastermind, and giant battleship pilot. Wood seems obvious for Nonon since it has Performance but my intuition say it fits Sanageyama better; I think Nonon would work well as a Fire Aspect who favors Performance. Iori, who's passively sitting back and handling the R&amp;D end of things when he's not leading covert strikes, probably works as an Air Aspect.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Ragyo works well as an Infernal, although she could be an immensely powerful Exigent of the life fibers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nui is probably spot-on for a Liminal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree except Nonon. She is clearly Air she was first one who could fly and she is using sound attacks which usually fits to air (eventhough sound travel slowest in air odd pairing) Sanageyama is an obvious wood even his style with wooden sword fits to that theme but he can be easily a fire aspect considering his reckless charges once in a while and he is most combat oriented of four deva's but if I would put someone for fire aspect it would be Satsuki especially close to ending.<br /> <br /> Iori would be an Exigent of sewing since we never saw him fighting and just stay in the back.<br /> <br /> For Nui and Ragyo alchemical would also work considering Nui's background it also fits to be an alchemical we don't really know how and when Ragyo got her life-fibers so it is a little hard to say anything for her.<br /> <br /> For Ryuko consdiering her background and after birth incidents I think Abyssal is a good fit and Mako being her lunar mate could explain the ending of last episode along with all of Mako behaviours. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mako's brother would be a night caste favoring larceny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2468-silentshadow","name":"SilentShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2468_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T15:31:43-07:00","id":100905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100728#post100728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is Nui's not on this list? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is an infectious mind virus that will torment you with sleepless nights.<br /> <br /> (Nui's theme probably stands out in comparison to the others in that it's significantly boosted when heard in a staggered manner; the light, eerie early points when she's wandering around dissonantly making cheery comments on the proceedings, and then the big heavy part in the context of her literally dropping into the story to throw everything off the rails)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T15:39:43-07:00","id":100912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished Episode 6. Best foe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prepare to be surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:33:24-07:00","id":100946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100873#post100873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand. I asked if people stopped watching porn, because I was getting tired of people who can't accept that some stories have the audacity to use nudity as a medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd probably have less reaction against nudity in stories if nudity didn't have a way of replacing story.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the way the characters dress is a tremendous turn-off for a lot of folks who assume it's a thinly-veiled porno. Sure, there's some very clever stuff behind that, but first impressions count for a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:49:27-07:00","id":100957,"title":"","content":"What the-Oh no! THE DAY OF JDUGMENT HAS COME! <i>They've unleashed the Exalted Forum on the rest of us!</i><br /> <br /> RUN FOR YOUR LIVES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:58:07-07:00","id":100962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100946#post100946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd probably have less reaction against nudity in stories if nudity didn't have a way of replacing story.<br /> <br /> Frankly, the way the characters dress is a tremendous turn-off for a lot of folks who assume it's a thinly-veiled porno. Sure, there's some very clever stuff behind that, but first impressions count for a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, my first reaction to an entirely black cast of characters is that it's gonna be a gangster flick, but if I go out and say that entirely black cast is off-putting to me, I'd be called racist. And that would be true, because that would be racist!<br /> <br /> But when people get offended at nudity being used to develop a story, that's ok...<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich puts forth an interesting question! If someone who discriminates against other races is a racist, is someone who discriminates against nudity... A nudist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-28-2014, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:15:26-07:00","id":100971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100534#post100534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every refined prince of Hell needs to walk into the room to the strains of <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oWhcTesRFq0\" target=\"_blank\">Blumenkranz</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I put this question to you, gentlemen: what is Exaltation?!&quot;<br /> &quot;Exaltation is sin! Humanity's original sin!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:18:19-07:00","id":100976,"title":"","content":"Kill la Kill is definitely great, but I am 100% on board with anybody who is just absolutely turned off by its prominent visuals, halfway clever ties of it into overall theme of symbolic associations with clothing and personal identity or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T23:58:58-07:00","id":101112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=100976#post100976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kill la Kill is definitely great, but I am 100% on board with anybody who is just absolutely turned off by its prominent visuals, halfway clever ties of it into overall theme of symbolic associations with clothing and personal identity or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable, but also a little unfortunate as Kill la Kill is basically something of a deconstruction of fanservice in anime - &quot;Let's take a show about a girl who wears skimpy clothing and strips people, and then have Ryuuko act like most anybody would when they find themself wearing skimping clothing, have people actually call her out on what she's wearing, and make a setting where clothing itself is a bad guy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I mean, the entire point of the show is that this is a world in which clothing itself is evil. Nudists are good. You'll notice that Ragyo's ultimate outfit covered her entire body. And when Ryuuko was mind controlled by Junketsu, it covered much more of her body than Senketsu had. If you want to avoid being mind controlled by the evil clothing, you can't wear anything that covers too much of your body. Characters have to wear skimpy or no clothing if they want to win. By the end of the last episode everyone on the entire planet is butt nekkid.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So people who avoid Kill la Kill because of the fanservice are sort of like people who don't want to watch Madoka Magica because they don't like magical girl shows - since magical girl shows are made for little kids and are about cute girls doing cute things.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's entirely understandable that someone would see a screenshot of Ryuuko in her battle clothing, go with their first impression, say, &quot;Meh, just another Japanese porno-cartoon,&quot; and write it off.<br /> <br /> Just a little unfortunate since I've never seen a more intelligence use of fanservice worked into a show, and doubt I'll see it again any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-29-2014, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T03:08:48-07:00","id":101167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101112#post101112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So people who avoid Kill la Kill because of the fanservice are sort of like people who don't want to watch Madoka Magica because they don't like magical girl shows - since magical girl shows are made for little kids and are about cute girls doing cute things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would dispute this, at least when you add that extra note of specificity; Madoka Magica, in its implementation, doesn't actually have cutesy stuff.<br /> <br /> Kill la Kill, while clever, does actually have some of the visuals, so there's still stuff one has to look at that might still feel offputting.<br /> <br /> For myself, it's stretched a little too close during episode 9 when there's stuff like Ryuko hanging by her straps, which are stretched right out, and when she's being pummeled with gratuitous shots (and yes, a person monologuing does draw the attention of the shot somewhat, but it's still <i>present</i>, and you'd still have to see it).<br /> <br /> Kill la Kill frames shots to have these visuals a lot less than plain fanservice shows would, but a bit more then I'd like, and enough that I am fully understanding of it turning off anybody who just plain doesn't like to see those things.<br /> <br /> Really, the better comparison to Madoka Magica is for people who just plain don't like visuals of stylized cute girls in frilly outfits*, no matter what they're doing. That's what I ultimately found to be why my siblings couldn't get into it; they're just not compelled by something that looks like that.<br /> <br /> I can hardly disagree with that, and there can be even more behind being repelled by fanservice visuals than that, so it's something that I just cannot dispute.<br /> <br /> * I'm also driven to recall that somebody on this forum once said that, for all its quality, they ultimately didn't like it because they don't like seeing shows of young girls being put through traumatic experiences or having to go through extreme self-sacrifices, and that's another approach for &quot;I don't care how good it is or clever it's being, I can't actually bear watching it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T03:13:07-07:00","id":101169,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, apparently there's going to be one last part to the series, an OVA to be released in September.<br /> <br /> Just when I think I'm out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T04:16:58-07:00","id":101183,"title":"","content":"Well, saying &quot;I can't watch this because x&quot; is perfectly reasonable and acceptable. People have preferences and bad experiences. I myself have problems watching anything that presents very religious characters as role models and protagonists. Hell, I can't watch anything with Ben Stiller in it, because after watching Night in Museum I expect to see a travesty like that each time I see his stupid face, which was very unfortunate for The Secrete Life of Walter Mitty, which I couldn't properly enjoy and which many people consider a really good movie.<br /> <br /> But it's very different then saying &quot;This &lt;insert media here&gt; is objecively bad, because it uses x as a medium to tell a story and no &lt;insert media here&gt; should ever use x to tell a story&quot;. People who say first about Kill la Kill, like Isator I assume, are justified. People who say the second need to just shut up. It's literally like saying books are bad because they have written text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 03-29-2014, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:46:00-07:00","id":101256,"title":"","content":"i have problems to watch mecha themed animes, i really dont like that type of animes, that didnt keep me off from watching TTGL, gundam series, code geass, infinite stratos, break blade and many more, people that complains from some animes due to some pictures or because they didnt liked the first chapter dont know how to apreciate good animes, i.e. steins gate, the images make the show look like another review of life anime, and the first 6 chapters are boring as hell, but after that, is one of the most amazing animes you can find.<br /> <br /> same thing with this type of fanservice shows, i really enjoyed ikkitousen, not for her dress explisions, but for her BG history, same with KLK, at least they make fanservice and manservice be part of the main history and not a way to get more viewers, and they did it very well i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:06:19-07:00","id":101265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elyon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101256#post101256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">people that complains from some animes due to some pictures or because they didnt liked the first chapter dont know how to apreciate good animes</div> </div> </div> </div>This, this is the kind of attitude I'm trying to avoid, because Jesus Christ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:13:27-07:00","id":101270,"title":"","content":"surprisingly enough, the one that everyone points out as too fan servicey and stuff, Queen's Blade has a very involved storyline and plot and the world is a matriarchy. Sure there is fanservice but if you look just at the plot you will find that it is one of the better fantasy anime out there. Highschool DXD falls into the same category, lots of fanservice but a good amount of substance. Its also very self aware of what happens in the show. I just found it rather humorous and ironic that the crowd that I've seen and interact with who tend towards feminism are drawn to KLK but truly dislike QB or other shows with fanservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:15:45-07:00","id":101273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101265#post101265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, this is the kind of attitude I'm trying to avoid, because Jesus Christ.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's at least partially true. Japanese anime is build on conventions (like all of Japanese cultures) that are by large unbreakable. To look at those conventions and condemn this form of media because it uses them is exactly like, and I hate to repeat myself yet again, condemning books for having written text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:19:52-07:00","id":101418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101167#post101167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would dispute this, at least when you add that extra note of specificity; Madoka Magica, in its implementation, doesn't actually have cutesy stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm just remembering when I urged my friend to watch it. <br /> <br /> Him: &quot;What, it's a magical girl show?'<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;Well yeah. But it's not like most magical girl shows. It's pretty dark. You'll like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Him: &quot;Look man. I don't like magical girl shows...&quot;<br /> <br /> He watches <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IoYoQT6Lje4\" target=\"_blank\">the opening</a> and calls me back to tell me he dropped it. &quot;Nope, not interested.&quot;<br /> <br /> I eventually convinced him to watch it - I told him that if he did and didn't like it, I'd buy him $50 in booze at the bar the next week. <br /> <br /> He texts me a couple hours later, &quot;Wow. This is kind of hardcore.&quot; Then calls me the next day at 3 in the morning drunk and crying his heart out. &quot;Homura's a hero! She's a fucking hero!&quot; Waaaahaaaahaaaa... Why can't she be happy? Waaaaaaaa...&quot;<br /> <br /> It was kind of fun.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I can't blame people who see something Madoka's opening, get the wrong impression and write it off. And I can't blame people who see a screenshot of Ryuuko's ass and decide not to bother with. <br /> <br /> Kill la Kill uses fan service, but it does so in a way that the vast majority of series don't, and approaches the subject matter in a smarter way than most series. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101270#post101270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">surprisingly enough, the one that everyone points out as too fan servicey and stuff, Queen's Blade has a very involved storyline and plot and the world is a matriarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, I actually enjoyed Queen's Blade a lot. The setting was kind of interesting, and it had some fantastic characters; Ymir is one of my favorite characters I've seen in anime. The episode where she was selling weapons to the bandits attacking her travelling companion was priceless. And the Egyptian Queen was really fun too - some day I want to make an Exalted character based on her. Though after what happened to Nowa in the most recent OVA... I probably won't be watching the show anymore, if it does get another season. <br /> <br /> But anyway, the fanservice in Queen's Blade was just blatant fanservice. And they were really in your face about it; especially the Holy Poses (I actually felt a little embarrassed when those would come on the screen). Hell, even Seikon no Qwazar had a reason for why there were tits everywhere. But in Queen's Blade the boobs are there just to sell DVDs.11<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:05:32-07:00","id":101441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101418#post101418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But anyway, the fanservice in Queen's Blade was just blatant fanservice. And they were really in your face about it; especially the Holy Poses (I actually felt a little embarrassed when those would come on the screen). Hell, even Seikon no Qwazar had a reason for why there were tits everywhere. But in Queen's Blade the boobs are there just to sell DVDs.11</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem of fanservice in Queeen's Blade is that it's bad for the same reason that too much expoction is bad in Shamaylan's movies- it serves no point whatsoever. It pisses me the hell off that those characters are running around 80% naked, without so much as making a point about it. The fanservice is just sort of... There. Without ever being acknowledged by the cast and I dunno, it just completely breakes my immersion.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen of Kill la Kill, the nudity is used to develop a story. I wouldn't even call it fanservice at this point, it's not just there for your enjoyment, it's an actual part of the storyline. If you remove it, Kill la Kill wouldn't be able to tell the story it's trying to tell, it's completely necessary. To call the series out on it and claim that it's bad because it has sexualization and objectification is just... Ignorant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:27:35-07:00","id":101463,"title":"","content":"Kill la Kill has fanservice... really?<br /> <br /> Hadn't noticed.<br /> <br /> Too busy snorting its 120% batshit crazy awesome up my nose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2594-solomon-black","name":"Solomon Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T06:22:01-07:00","id":101890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101441#post101441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem of fanservice in Queeen's Blade is that it's bad for the same reason that too much expoction is bad in Shamaylan's movies- it serves no point whatsoever. It pisses me the hell off that those characters are running around 80% naked, without so much as making a point about it. The fanservice is just sort of... There. Without ever being acknowledged by the cast and I dunno, it just completely breakes my immersion.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen of Kill la Kill, the nudity is used to develop a story. I wouldn't even call it fanservice at this point, it's not just there for your enjoyment, it's an actual part of the storyline. If you remove it, Kill la Kill wouldn't be able to tell the story it's trying to tell, it's completely necessary. To call the series out on it and claim that it's bad because it has sexualization and objectification is just... Ignorant.</div> </div> </div> </div>so, because you like one, its not fanservice but you don't like the other so its fanservice. What's so bad about fanservice anyways? The only thing I see catch this much flak for it is anime. Game of Thrones spends almost 25 minutes each episode showing tits and bush. No one bitches there. Same thing with True Blood and many many other shows heralded and referred to as fantastic. <br /> <br /> Also no one said KLK was bad. No one here did. I'm not watching it, I dropped it until the hype cools down and I do that every season with the overhyped normal folks show (SNK, SAO, S;G, Chuu2, Madoka just to name a few). and here comes another controversial statement. TTGL isn't that great. Its okay. The only reason everyone latched onto it is because they had never seen any of the super robot shows that predated it and which it took huge amounts of content from. Gao Gai Gar which came out in the 90s is so damn similar its eerie and its better (until they break all suspension of disbelief by hurling galaxies at each other {inb4 'suspension of dlisbelief with super robots hurrr})","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T07:30:51-07:00","id":101913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101890#post101890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I see catch this much flak for it is anime. Game of Thrones spends almost 25 minutes each episode showing tits and bush. No one bitches there. Same thing with True Blood and many many other shows heralded and referred to as fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no I've seen exactly those kinds of criticisms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T07:45:36-07:00","id":101917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101913#post101913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no I've seen exactly those kinds of criticisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>never seen that here on these forums or in real life, or anywhere for that matter. You must associate with much different people than I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:19:08-07:00","id":101941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101917#post101917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> never seen that here on these forums or in real life, or anywhere for that matter. You must associate with much different people than I.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://www.google.co.uk/search?q=game+of+thrones+sexposition&amp;ie=UTF-8&amp;oe=UTF-8&amp;hl=en-gb&amp;client=safari\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.co.uk/search?q=ga...&amp;client=safari</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:42:09-07:00","id":101950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101890#post101890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, because you like one, its not fanservice but you don't like the other so its fanservice. What's so bad about fanservice anyways? The only thing I see catch this much flak for it is anime. Game of Thrones spends almost 25 minutes each episode showing tits and bush. No one bitches there. Same thing with True Blood and many many other shows heralded and referred to as fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, maybe I'll say it like this: fanservice in Queen's Blade is like explosions in Micheal Bay's movies- it doesn't serve to advence a story, in fact it does nothing for the story, it's there bcause people like seeing explosions in the background. The fact that the cast of Queen's Blade is running half-naked is not what buggs me, it's that nobody seems to notice. It's like it's a part of daily life rutine for them and sorry, I just can't treat it seriously. I can't get into it, because my immerison is immediately broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:57:17-07:00","id":101999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101950#post101950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe I'll say it like this: fanservice in Queen's Blade is like explosions in Micheal Bay's movies- it doesn't serve to advence a story, in fact it does nothing for the story, it's there bcause people like seeing explosions in the background. The fact that the cast of Queen's Blade is running half-naked is not what buggs me, it's that nobody seems to notice. It's like it's a part of daily life rutine for them and sorry, I just can't treat it seriously. I can't get into it, because my immerison is immediately broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Michael Bay is one of the most entertaining film makers on the planet and an unappreciated genius of mayhem. While indeed they only occasionally advance the logic diagram of the story, they almost always advance the entertainment.<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yj9yt1M7S-8\" target=\"_blank\"> Case In Point.</a><br /> <br /> You don't have to take my word for it, just check his box offices recepits. Clearly he has a good and reliable grasp of what the public wants to see and spend money on. And that makes him a veritable national treasure we would all be sorely deprived to be without.<br /> <br /> Something something popularity doesn't matter coming my way right no?<br /> <br /> That's nice really... but why should I give you a 100+ million dollars to make a movie merely based on your opinion that doesn't need to show tangible results? And then when it turns out that however &quot;good&quot; your movie is whatever awards and accolades it may have won... I'm broke because I didn't make my money back meaning literally enough people did not agree with your definition of good to be worth my 100+ million dollars. And it doesn't stop there of course. See because I didn't make my money back I now don't have it to support the next genius idea to come my way. Financial failure directly effects every other potential work in the industry. Not to mention the Mongol horde of people that get a name in the credits and a middle class-ish income from my 100+ million dollars. Now they are all out of a job! You monster!<br /> <br /> So popularity is the most important thing for entertainment, because its the only thing that is going to get your brilliant good idea made.<br /> <br /> Now is Kill la Kill popular.... well its certainly more popular then a lot of anime. Look there was enough critical mass in the nerddom to wash over into this forum, a completely unrelated subject matter. I can find other indicators but all of them indicate the Kill la Kill had been pretty damn popular. Do you have counter-indications? Not hypothetical could have been rhetorical arguments but actual factual results.<br /> <br /> Or to really put it briefly... does sex NOT sell?<br /> <br /> If sex sells then you should only expect fanservice because its what's the market clearly wants and supports. Least the anime market that isn't going for kids methinks. Whether you care for it or not personally is simply irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Me personally after I realized several years ago I was a damn hypocrite that parroted all the negative statements about fanservice like a good little boy... but well I already showed my hand. I never put my money were my mouth was and actually either stopped watching or avoided something because of fanservice. Heck I sought them out all the same, so why was I speaking against them or implying I'd somehow like them better without sexy sexy people running around in them? Because the truth is I wouldn't. I would not enjoy these sorts of silly nonsense stories nearly as much if the people were not 'dressed' in stylistic nudity. Fanservice isn't always appropriate, but for Kill la Kill and hell... probably most shonen silly crazy anime it is. I happen to like nearly naked people running around, it congeals well with the unreality of it all when they look sexier then would ever be possible.<br /> <br /> Yes I enjoy my fanservice and only thing I'm tired of is annoying haters implying I should feel shame when clearly more people agree with me then them. Heck I think I even enjoy it in men because I appreciate a nicely sculpted human body male or female. Fave manga right now... has a <a href=\"http://www.zerochan.net/1664541#full\" target=\"_blank\">lotta dudes occaisonally dressed like this</a> in it and I like it just fine. I'd be totally down for more sexy dudes around but... doesn't seem to be quite the same market for that so I can't really expect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2594-solomon-black","name":"Solomon Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:16:56-07:00","id":102013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=101999#post101999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to take my word for it, just check his box offices recepits. Clearly he has a good and reliable grasp of what the public wants to see and spend money on. And that makes him a veritable national treasure we would all be sorely deprived to be without.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really no. It makes him a national resource, not a treasure. A thing of value to be used while it has value, it doesn't make his stuff good, it makes his stuff valuable.<br /> <br /> McDonanlds sells far more hamburgers than the finest restaurants, therefore McDonalds hamburgers are the best and something to be treasured. The logic doesn't flow there, nor does it follow with Michael Bay's works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:43:55-07:00","id":102027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102013#post102013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really no. It makes him a national resource, not a treasure. A thing of value to be used while it has value, it doesn't make his stuff good, it makes his stuff valuable.<br /> <br /> McDonanlds sells far more hamburgers than the finest restaurants, therefore McDonalds hamburgers are the best and something to be treasured. The logic doesn't flow there, nor does it follow with Michael Bay's works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something something popularity doesn't matter coming my way right no?<br /> <br /> That's nice really... but why should I give you a 100+ million dollars to make a movie merely based on your opinion that doesn't need to show tangible results? And then when it turns out that however &quot;good&quot; your movie is whatever awards and accolades it may have won... I'm broke because I didn't make my money back meaning literally enough people did not agree with your definition of good to be worth my 100+ million dollars. And it doesn't stop there of course. See because I didn't make my money back I now don't have it to support the next genius idea to come my way. Financial failure directly effects every other potential work in the industry. Not to mention the Mongol horde of people that get a name in the credits and a middle class-ish income from my 100+ million dollars. Now they are all out of a job! You monster!<br /> <br /> So popularity is the most important thing for entertainment, because its the only thing that is going to get your brilliant good idea made.<br /> <br /> Yes I just copyapasta'd myself. I've heard your argument so many times I no longer need to wait for it.<br /> <br /> And McDonalds... same damn thing really.<br /> It may well not be the best burger ever, but clearly more people like their food then don't so the company must have been doing <i>something</i> right all this time. You can tell by their high levels of success. Their food gives me gas and the runs personally so even though I like the taste I don't care for the aftermath, but my solution is rather simple. I don't eat there and I don't complain about those that do. Who am I to tell them their food is crap, what makes me so much wiser and nobler I should make up other people's minds for them? And presuming that people are capable of making up their own damn minds then eventually if McDonalds isn't what people want it will fold in good time. I don't have to do anything I've already won by default by simply not eating there.<br /> <br /> Status Quo is the status quo for damned good reasons.<br /> <br /> Want to change it? Knock yourself out! I don't have a gun to your head do I? I'm not gonna help just 'cuz you said so of course. Don't need to I'm winning already remember. But if I was out to change the status quo I would probably start by understanding why more people like fanservice, Michael Bay, and McDonalds then those that don't so I can persuade them from their perspective not force my perspective on them. And if I'm not doing that... well talk is cheap what exactly am I doing then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2594-solomon-black","name":"Solomon Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:56:31-07:00","id":102034,"title":"","content":"The status quo is not always the status quo for damned good reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T