l=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Want to change it? Knock yourself out! I don't have a gun to your head do I? I'm not gonna help just 'cuz you said so of course. Don't need to I'm winning already remember. But if I was out to change the status quo I would probably start by understanding why more people like fanservice, Michael Bay, and McDonalds then those that don't so I can persuade them from their perspective not force my perspective on them. And if I'm not doing that... well talk is cheap what exactly am I doing then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that people are pigs in human clothing and that you have to control them with explosions and tits? If so then say it! Embrace your courage and flash it proudly, let it shine in the night sky for gods to see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T15:19:19-07:00","id":102200,"title":"","content":"Okay, so now I want to switch away from my prior points about defense of people who would dislike Kill la Kill in favour of more stuff that I myself actually liked about it.<br /> <br /> Or anything else on the planet besides what this thread is doing right now, I'm not too picky...<br /> <br /> So, one of the things that initially drew me was in how the protagonist was a woman, though still with basically all of the attitudes of your typical shonen protagonist, but part of what kept me very closely drawn in was how it had a variety of prominent (and incidental) female characters, with a diversity in personalities and relationships, and good development in each, without relying very heavily on stereotypes. That, really, is what helps me over some of the more overt visuals, more than the idea that they're running with a coherent theme under it all; whatever they're being put through, there are real characters underneath it. The Bechdel test isn't as utterly comprehensive as some people who point to it might imply, but the series still does entirely well with it; I mean, bonus points for how almost every female character has a connection to and conversations (or at least exchanged words with) every other female character.<br /> <br /> This even extends nicely to how, although romance in general isn't really prominent, and is mostly left in implications, the most prominent implied romantic connections between characters are between women, but without it needing to be all showy and titillating.<br /> <br /> And it gets to do all this without also making it a story that excludes men entirely, as many such seem to feel the need to. Like, there are women, and there are men, and the women get to just happen to be more prominent in the overall story.<br /> <br /> This is all a matter relevant to my interests, so to see a show do so well with it in terms of character and story is very satisfying to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T15:28:43-07:00","id":102207,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Calm down folks. No need for this to get out of hand. Thank you in advance.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T17:06:00-07:00","id":102255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102200#post102200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so now I want to switch away from my prior points about defense of people who would dislike Kill la Kill in favour of more stuff that I myself actually liked about it.<br /> <br /> Or anything else on the planet besides what this thread is doing right now, I'm not too picky...</div> </div> </div> </div>+1<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This even extends nicely to how, although romance in general isn't really prominent, and is mostly left in implications, the most prominent implied romantic connections between characters are between women, but without it needing to be all showy and titillating. </div> </div> </div>I've got to disagree, here. Gamagoori Ira and Mankanshoku Mako are hands-down the most implied romantic connection in the series.<br /> <br /> In the end credits, Gamagoori is dressed up in a white tuxedo holding a bouquet of flowers as he waits for Mako to walk around the corner. He took a blade to the gut for her and passed out only after he saw she was alright. He made her family a personal vow to save her from the Covers. In Episode 23, Mako's mother makes Gamagoori croquettes fashioned to look like Mako's face.<br /> <br /> <br /> By far, though, Mako and Ryuuko's friendship is more important to the plot, as is Ryuuko's intense and evolving relationship with Satsuki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T17:56:14-07:00","id":102279,"title":"","content":"I would view that as more <u>overt</u>, but not more prominent. I'm judging prominence in terms of the importance of characters and relationships in overall narrative and characterisation.<br /> <br /> That said, the only characters we ever see actually kissing are both women.<br /> <br /> Just to branch off of this point, another mild feather I'd put in the show's cap is the fact that, to the extent that romantic attractions are implied, the idea of women liking women is apparent, but incidental and unremarked upon. Neither characters nor framing of the narrative treat it as any more unusual than women and men, it's just... there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T18:31:23-07:00","id":102288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102279#post102279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would view that as more <u>overt</u>, but not more prominent. I'm judging prominence in terms of the importance of characters and relationships in overall narrative and characterisation.<br /> <br /> That said, the only characters we ever see actually kissing are both women.<br /> <br /> Just to branch off of this point, another mild feather <b>I'd put in the show's cap is the fact that, to the extent that romantic attractions are implied, the idea of women liking women is apparent, but incidental and unremarked upon. Neither characters nor framing of the narrative treat it as any more unusual than women and men, it's just... there.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thats actually very common in anime/manga, actual Japanese culture differs a bit (the japanese view of homosexuality isn't driven by religious hatred or anything of that matter, but the typical japanese person views homosexuality as a deviation. And like many things of this nature is typically handled in a humorous fashion, very tongue in cheek.) Yuri and yaoi pairings in anime/manga tend to be very candid and unless a friend is teasing another friend about it (not like rude teasing but playful teasing, I doubt I need to clarify this but someone may misunderstand) its typically left be. You can see this in most shows with a focus on yuri or yaoi. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T23:46:47-07:00","id":102450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102279#post102279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would view that as more <u>overt</u>, but not more prominent. I'm judging prominence in terms of the importance of characters and relationships in overall narrative and characterisation.<br /> <br /> That said, the only characters we ever see actually kissing are both women.<br /> <br /> Just to branch off of this point, another mild feather I'd put in the show's cap is the fact that, to the extent that romantic attractions are implied, the idea of women liking women is apparent, but incidental and unremarked upon. Neither characters nor framing of the narrative treat it as any more unusual than women and men, it's just... there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should probably watch more anime. As far as Kill la Kill goes, it's scrapping the bottom of the barrel. Most anime in fact have tons of implied homosexual relationships. I also have yet to find a single anime in which anti-homosexual stance is glorified in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T00:10:33-07:00","id":102467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102027#post102027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something something popularity doesn't matter coming my way right no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really no. You used a definition incorrectly, I pointed out how it was incorrect. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102027#post102027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nice really... but why should I give you a 100+ million dollars to make a movie merely based on your opinion that doesn't need to show tangible results?</div> </div> </div> </div> Something I in no way suggested or advocated. Please stop shoving words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102027#post102027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I just copyapasta'd myself. I've heard your argument so many times I no longer need to wait for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you have heard the correction so many times, I'm mildly surprised you insist on disagreeing with it and then claiming people have said things they have not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=102027#post102027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Want to change it? Knock yourself out! I don't have a gun to your head do I? I'm not gonna help just 'cuz you said so of course.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your sudden choice to veer in the direction of implied violence here is highly disturbing. You might want to refine your comments in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now I at no time implied or stated that Michael Bay's films shouldn't be produced. As you yourself mentioned they net millions up to the low billions range. If it's what people want, it's what they are willing to pay for, then it's what they shall get and everyone is happy. It's important to recognize however that they're not great movies that will still be watched in any great amount in the future. Again, that's fine. <br /> <br /> However, the major studios also recognize that much like venture capital investing, you periodically need to invest in films that look like they're going to flop out of the gate. Because they might turn into highly profitable movies, and possibly even ones that turn into profitable lines. Star Wars is the classic example of that, they had to bundle it with a romance movie in order to get theaters to play it... and then of course it became popular and evolved into the franchise we have today. The Sixth Sense was much the same, it's still a popular film but it had little belief it was going to go anywhere from the studios. And then of course there are the &quot;sleeper&quot; successes, such as My Big Fat Greek Wedding, which met with absolutely abysmal box office numbers only to massively spike after the fact. Or even something like Blair Witch Project which was little more than a college art school film project and it netted around a quarter billion.<br /> <br /> Point is, it's like any other business. You put the 90% cash into the stuff you have the greatest certainty that people will buy. You put 10% on the longshots. Because like venture capitalism, 90% of them will fail, but the 10% that don't will do well and potentially lead to new stuff to exploit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T05:52:41-07:00","id":102579,"title":"","content":"My experience of anime, which is... fairly large, tends to see the approach to homosexuality (particularly with women) in any story that is not directly about a romance in terms of either being coded (that is to say, implied by certain resonant motifs verging on stereotypes), or being presented with a bit of melodrama. I've seen little that would take the idea as granted without making a big deal of it.<br /> <br /> Still, that could just mean things that are comparable have slipped by me. I'd be interested in any examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:19:10-07:00","id":102633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Holy shit, what the fuck is this explicit incestuous rape narrative going on between Ragyou and Satsuki? jesus christ that was not okay</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm never quite sure what to make of that part. All I can say is that I do not quite find it instinctively repellent, so there might be some place for it, but I'm not really sure how to articulate it, and it's not something I really care to find that articulation*.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, more than anything else, if it was to be something anybody honed in on as a dealbreaker, I'd be willing to err on the side of sensitivity.<br /> <br /> * Although dammit, now I am thinking of it in terms that are actually coming up as words in my mind. I suppose... it might <i>kind of</i> intersect vaguely with the angle on this subject I've mentioned before concerning &quot;honesty&quot;; that a person like that would be exploitative of such a relationship. There, it's out of my head now, let me have nothing more to say on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T08:42:37-07:00","id":102649,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that at least part of the point is that Ragyou is <i>really fucking creepy</i>, so they had her doing the creepiest thing they could think. There is more depth to it one could analyze, but it does serve to quickly give Ragyou more characterization as a terrible, creepy, exploitative monster. In light of what happens later in the show, it also serves as characterization for Satsuki, demonstrating how she is willing to get through horrible things to achieve her goal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T16:50:08-07:00","id":103001,"title":"","content":"Okay, one last word:<br /> <br /> There can be problems with the matter of appropriation with that idea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be perhaps a bit more concise on this point, as well on exactly what the sense of ambiguity I referred to previously is: I'm never quite sure whether or not to take Ragyou as the usual lazy &quot;rape as easy way to establish character as evil&quot;, which has all kinds of problems relating to trivializing the realities of rape, or an actual halfway decent insight into the circumstances of somebody being sexually abused by somebody they are closely associated with.<br /> <br /> I... <i>extremely</i> tentatively lean ever so slightly in the direction of the latter, based on surrounding details; Ragyou is sexually abusive towards Satsuki, but initially still kind of... motherly towards her. It's messed up, but possibly messed up in the way that sexually abusive parents might be. That Ragyou at that time seems kind of sincere in her regard for Satsuki, well, I feel it might lend a bit of credibility to the possibility that there's a bit more nuance to the portrayal than it just being an easy shorthand for Ragyou being evil.<br /> <br /> I guess that might be part of why I'm not inherently repelled by the scenes in question, although this whole line of discussion is making me feel very uncomfortable as I try to sort out my thoughts. There's a part of me which is examining this in terms of not wanting certain uncomfortable realities to be culturally invisible, which is struggling against the need to be share that the basic outlines aren't being exploited for cheap narrative purposes, with a dash of &quot;I don't want it to be invisible, but there are places where visibility is not appropriate&quot;. I can't find an easy answer to it.<br /> <br /> (There are also problems for what it means for the writing of Satsuki as well; if &quot;villain is a rapist&quot; is a cheap and lazy way to convey evil, then &quot;badass women is current or prior victim of sexual abuse or assault&quot; is a cheap way to provide credentials (or relatability or the like) to a character, and I might be worried about that being at play as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-31-2014, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:29:47-07:00","id":103517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, what the fuck is this explicit incestuous rape narrative going on between Ragyou and Satsuki? jesus christ that was not okay</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's kind of the point, no? It's not a &quot;sin&quot; to display something disturbing for what it is.<br /> <br /> For it to be a &quot;Sin&quot;, it would have to be displayed in a manner that condones the act. Calling what the show did betweenRagyo and Satsuki a sin is similar to calling a documentary on murder a sin. because it shows murder. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:56:09-07:00","id":103592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=103517#post103517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For it to be a &quot;Sin&quot;, it would have to be displayed in a manner that condones the act.</div> </div> </div> </div>urrrrrggh goddammit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:44:56-07:00","id":103651,"title":"","content":"Two episodes in, and I have rolled my eyes <i>far</i> less than I expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T16:17:24-07:00","id":103697,"title":"","content":"Run with that feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:43:09-07:00","id":103729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=103001#post103001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Ragyou at that time seems kind of sincere in her regard for Satsuki, well, I feel it might lend a bit of credibility to the possibility that there's a bit more nuance to the portrayal than it just being an easy shorthand for Ragyou being evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it a bit more believable that Ragyou is a thorough narcissist, and that whatever she does to Satsuki is for her own personal enjoyment rather than any motherly affection. That is, she molests Satsuki first of all because Satsuki looks like her, and because it amuses Ragyo's sadism.<br /> <br /> We ARE talking about the woman who experimented on her firstborn child as a baby, repeated the experiment on the next baby at a younger age, and then tossed that second child into the trash when it died.<br /> <br /> Also, remember how Nui sewed Houhoumaru Rei into Ragyo's final kamui? We should also remember that Nui explicitly stated in earlier episodes that she and Ragyo were intending to feed Satsuki to that kamui instead. Only Satsuki escaped and Rei pissed off Nui, so Nui used Rei instead.<br /> <br /> Ragyo only loves the second daughter and Nui to the extent that they are like her -- Life Fiber hybrids that she can use for her own goals. The more that the second daughter refused to obey, the more Ragyo writes her off again as a waste of flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T02:20:55-07:00","id":103924,"title":"","content":"Sooo, other things to talk about...<br /> <br /> One of the things I quite like about the action is that it's got the same kind of frenetic energy Gurren Lagann had, but I feel like the premise gives it more versatility in playing it out, and that it's being done directly by human characters rather than mechas gives it a better sense of flow and urgency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T05:12:23-07:00","id":103970,"title":"","content":"My favorite thing was the little animation bits. <br /> <br /> Like here with Nui<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://0-media-cdn.foolz.us/ffuuka/board/a/image/1387/55/1387554313810.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can see how at first she's dodging and having fun.. and then decides it would be more fun to act like she was scared and almost getting hit. <br /> <br /> Every scene is jam packed with little things like that - character's gazes or positions slowly moving to draw attention to something, or little hidden jokes or fun poses that just last for a single frame. <br /> <br /> You could tell the animators at Trigger had a lot of fun making this series. And I think that enjoyment and energy was passed on to the viewers really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T07:27:56-07:00","id":104805,"title":"","content":"You know, one thing I'm hopeful for, and surprisingly looking forward to, is what a dub of Kill la Kill would be like.<br /> <br /> It's actually put me in the mind to properly articulate what I see as the merit in dubs; I'll generally watch subs at this time just because it gives me a sense of nuances that are more firm in the subject, but when it's something this good, with such interesting characters, I really want to be able to find out what they'd be like with a voice that is more familiar to me.<br /> <br /> I mean, I just find myself unconsciously imagining just what the words of Ryuko or Satsuki or Ragyo would sound like in English, just to be able to cross a certain mild dissonance gap, and I feel very compelled by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:04:25-07:00","id":104822,"title":"","content":"Why did it take me this long to find out that the person who composed the Kill la Kill soundtrack is the same person as the Attack on Titan soundtrack?!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:09:26-07:00","id":105114,"title":"","content":"Gamagoori is just, like, the <i>best</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly bothered by the Crunchyroll translation of <i>Shitenn\u014d</i> being &quot;Elite Four.&quot; It's such a strange translation of the term, and <i>very</i> specific to Pok\u00e9mon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T23:26:53-07:00","id":105406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=104822#post104822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did it take me this long to find out that the person who composed the Kill la Kill soundtrack is the same person as the Attack on Titan soundtrack?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? That explains why Satsuki's theme is so freakin' badass. I can listen to those drums for ever. In fact I'm doing it right now! It's so good... And blumenkrantz speaks for itself of course.<br /> <br /> Anyway, concerning Ragyou's relationship with Satsuki, the bath scene was easily ma favourite of the series. I don't know, maybe I;'m just a huge sucker for incest in media in general, because I think it's both missrepresented and unexplored (fortunately anime has me covered on that front). I think in Kill la Kill it just sort of... Fits. It's one more thing they weren't afraid to use as a medium o tell a story and in Kill la Kill it simply works.<br /> <br /> I don't know how, but every relationship between characters is believable. All of them seem very natural, genuine even, which is very rare in media. There is no one relationship that doesn't seem to make sense. Even the horriblly abusive relationship of Ragyou and Satsuki, even if unpleasant, doesn't seem like a trick, it's something that I can really believe could happen and I think it's just the way they created all those characters and this universe as so interesting and so immersive that I just want these things to be real, even the most awful ones. I think this is a mark of great story!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T17:32:22-07:00","id":105924,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying some of the stylistic elements of this show, like how all computer screens are like old Gameboys, how flashbacks are in <i>redscale</i> and non-widescreen, and how the show uses the painted freeze frame look like it was going out of style.<br /> Also Gamagoori's obvious and deliberate case of Hokuto no Syndrome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:36:05-07:00","id":106485,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Two posts were causing problems with the page display. I've deleted them. This wasn't done because of content, but because of technical witchcraft.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:45:01-07:00","id":106570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=105924#post105924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">like how all computer screens are like old Gameboys</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that one is fun. It puts me curiously in mind of the apparently post-apocalyptic setting, like all the more advanced screen technology was wiped out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">, how flashbacks are in <i>redscale</i> and non-widescreen</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting to note how there are <i>so many</i> flashbacks; the show's pretty invested in conveying the backstories and motivations of a lot of the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:26:16-07:00","id":106604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=105924#post105924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Gamagoori's obvious and deliberate case of <b>Hokuto no Syndrome</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unfamiliar with this term, which I'm assuming has something to do with the fist of a certain star, but looking for it on google your post is apparently the only mention of it in the <i>entire internet</i>, so can I get some clarification, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T17:14:22-07:00","id":106620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=106604#post106604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unfamiliar with this term, which I'm assuming has something to do with the fist of a certain star, but looking for it on google your post is apparently the only mention of it in the <i>entire internet</i>, so can I get some clarification, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>No wonder, since the only other person who uses the term was the guy who present when I coined it<sup>1</sup>.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's when a character (typically a big one) keeps changing size, often between shots, with no regard for consistency. We named it after we noticed it happening to a random thug in the (first) Hokuto no Ken movie, who spent his entire screentime fluctuating wildly between <i>pretty big</i> and <i>gargantuan</i>.<br /> <br /> We needed a term for the phenomenon mostly because both of us keep doing it while roleplaying \u2013 if a character is bigger than average, we will eventually come to picture them as <i>arbitrarily enormous</i>.<br /> Once, he ended up getting the Giant Merit for a character halfway through a game, simply because we'd both started treating him as if he had it.<br /> <br /> <sub>1: I may have been present when <i>he</i> coined it. I forget.</sub>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:33:46-07:00","id":106649,"title":"","content":"Gamagoori's one is pretty weird, if in a fun way, since not only does it come across as a matter of framing and visual metaphor, there are actual moments when he interacts with other characters with his improbable size, anything from his finger being wider than Satsuki's entire hand to Jakuzure being able to stand comfortably on one of his shoulders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T20:22:00-07:00","id":106680,"title":"","content":"Over at Space Battles, we joke that Gamagoori's size is mathematically calculated as (You &lt; Gamagoori). Gamagoori is always Bigger Than You.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T13:17:20-07:00","id":107049,"title":"","content":"So, on the one hand, the final battle wasn't as rousing as that of TTGL. On the other, I think the show carried itself for longer than TTGL. Overall impression: very cool.<br /> <br /> I might have to rewatch it in short order, simply because I've fallen into a pattern of watching it daily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:06:48-07:00","id":107073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/100174-kill-la-kill?p=107049#post107049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, on the one hand, the final battle wasn't as rousing as that of TTGL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly not, although I personally prefer its rendition of &quot;everybody's helping out&quot;, in both phases.<br /> <br /> I also feel that Kill la Kill had something of a persistent theme of defeating tyranny not through overwhelming and actually beating it, but by continuously living in defiance of it, which might inform the ending a bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:54:21-07:00","id":107096,"title":"","content":"From an artistic perspective, Kill la Kill's final battle was probably the better-made of the two. Ragyo was certainly a better opponent than the Grand Zamboa, which just seemed to be symmetrical for symmetry's sake.<br /> <br /> Still, I distinctly recall how the finale of TTGL made me <i>feel</i>, bodily more than anything, and that just didn't happen here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:15:42-07:00","id":107105,"title":"","content":"Regarding last fights, I liked that in the TTGL OVA final battle there is more participation from the many people piloting the ultimate mecha, with it manifesting weapons suitable for each. However, I disliked the battle extending past what was the final, climatic blow of the original series. The transition was a <i>slightly</i> jarring despite their top notch animation and felt unnecessarily latched on. I just didn't feel is being as, I don't know, momentous as the effect of that original final, giving-it-all desperate attack","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T16:51:16-07:00","id":107145,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've seen that version of the fight. Chou Tengen Toppa Gurren Lagann <i>looks</i> cool, but that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T14:24:07-07:00","id":110286,"title":"","content":"More KlK crossover, <a href=\"http://algosky.deviantart.com/art/1-Cross-KLK